/api.github.com/users/mkouba/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"mentioned","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-07-27T21:31:27Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":7076669760,"node_id":"SE_lADOCFbutM5Or8VvzwAAAAGlzWlA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/events/7076669760","actor":{"login":"mkouba","id":913004,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzAwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913004?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba","html_url":"https://github.com/mkouba","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-07-27T21:31:27Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/1197805980","html_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/26975#issuecomment-1197805980","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/26975","id":1197805980,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCFbutM5HZRGc","user":{"login":"mkouba","id":913004,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzAwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913004?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba","html_url":"https://github.com/mkouba","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-28T08:05:38Z","updated_at":"2022-07-28T08:05:38Z","body":"Well, at the moment section parameters are whitespace-separated chunks where the equals sign is used to identify the optional name of a param.\r\n\r\nI.e. for `{#textInput field=\"username\" label=\"Username\"}`  the `SectionHelperFactory` for `textInput` receives two params. The first has a name `field` and the value is `\"username\"`. The second has name `label` and value `\"Username\"`. For `{#textInput field = \"username\" label = \"Username\"}` however, 6 params are parsed: [`field`, `=`, `\"username\"`, `label`, `=`, `\"Username\"`]. Also round brackets can be used to group several chunks (such as `{#if (item.active || item.sold) && item.enabled}`).\r\n\r\nThe `SectionHelperFactory` is then allowed to interpret these params in any way it needs to. So for example the `#if` section has a complex logic to turn the list of params into a condition.\r\n\r\nNow back to the problem. I do agree that the error message is confusing. And in this particular case the parser should be more lenient. We could probably treat the equals sign specially so that `field = \"username\"` is parsed as `field=\"username\"`. It would not be backward compatible but it shouldn't be a problem in most cases.\r\n\r\n> By default IDEs like InteliJ while formatting code are adding spaces around equal sign in templates.\r\n\r\nThat's unfortunate and I'm not sure whether it's actually reasonable.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/1197805980/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"mkouba","id":913004,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzAwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913004?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba","html_url":"https://github.com/mkouba","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":7079102262,"node_id":"AE_lADOCFbutM5Or8VvzwAAAAGl8oc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/events/7079102262","actor":{"login":"mkouba","id":913004,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzAwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913004?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"h